    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d557-a7">

                <pb facs="0622" n="542" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg542"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subinclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Translation of complaint.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Van</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1902-04-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 27,
                    1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">To the honorable the <hi rendition="#small-caps">English
                        Vice-Consul</hi>:</p>
                <p>In reply to your dispatch dated April 4, 1902, concerning the charge brought
                    against Dr. Ussher for the death of one Tahir, son of Aziz, corporal of
                    Hamidieh, of the district of Nordouse, who, it is claimed, died from an
                    operation performed on him by the said Dr. Ussher, we would say that the degree
                    of the charge will be decided after the examination into the case is made by the
                    assistant procurator of the appellate court.</p>
                <p>(Seal of the governor-general.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
